      "created": "2026-07-29T15:31:12.000Z",
      "id": 1138811,
      "npm_advisory_id": null,
      "overview": "nanoid (Nano ID) before 5.1.16 contains an infinite loop in the customAlphabet and nanoid functions of its non-secure module (nanoid/non-secure). When these functions are given a negative size, the loop counter is decremented from a negative value and never reaches its termination condition, spinning indefinitely and hanging the calling thread. An application that passes an unvalidated, attacker-controlled negative size to these functions is exposed to a denial-of-service condition.",
      "reported_by": null,
      "title": "nanoid: non-secure generators can loop indefinitely with negative size",
      "metadata": null,
      "cves": [
        "CVE-2026-67214"
      ],
      "access": "public",
      "severity": "high",
