      "references": "- https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-67213\n- https://github.com/ai/nanoid/commit/cb3626d0f3342fdf179cd425fd9c4fbb92c7d0e7\n- https://github.com/ai/nanoid/releases/tag/5.1.6\n- https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/nanoid-before-infinite-loop-via-zero-size-in-customalphabet-and-customrandom\n- https://github.com/ai/nanoid/commit/f9d13f150847d117877adee3460a46eceb0cf49b\n- https://github.com/ai/nanoid/releases/tag/3.3.17\n- https://github.com/ai/nanoid/commit/e10f8d40ce9d1ab47f66d65a16b48086432730d0\n- https://github.com/ai/nanoid/releases/tag/3.3.18\n- https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2v37-7h3g-55p8",
      "created": "2026-07-29T15:31:12.000Z",
      "id": 1139427,
      "npm_advisory_id": null,
      "overview": "nanoid (Nano ID) before 5.1.6 contains an infinite loop in the customAlphabet and customRandom functions. When these functions are configured with a size of 0, the internal generation loop never satisfies its exit condition and spins indefinitely, hanging the calling thread. An application that passes an unvalidated, attacker-controlled size of 0 to these functions is exposed to a denial-of-service condition.",
      "reported_by": null,
      "title": "nanoid: custom generators can loop indefinitely when size is zero",
      "metadata": null,
      "cves": [
        "CVE-2026-67213"
      ],
      "access": "public",
      "severity": "high",
      "module_name": "nanoid",
      "vulnerable_versions": "<3.3.18",
      "github_advisory_id": "GHSA-2v37-7h3g-55p8",
      "recommendation": "Upgrade to version 3.3.18 or later",
      "patched_versions": ">=3.3.18",
